From 67c3136d38288ff7fb54060bec5ff863419f4a35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redux Kernel Research <redux@invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:51:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm/panel: nv3052c: add Anbernic RG34XX-SP panel

Add the original panel of the Anbernic RG34XX-SP handheld (board strap
PE6 low): 3.4", 720x480, NV3052C controller, 24-bit parallel RGB.

The register table is the panel's complete sequence as the stock
Anbernic u-boot (U-Boot 2018.05) sends it, so the common registers are
skipped. One value differs: page 1 register 0x23 is 0x00 instead of
stock's 0xa2, to go with the active-low HSYNC/VSYNC timing used here;
stock pairs 0xa2 with active-high syncs and a longer frame. The same
sequence and timing (26 MHz, 60 Hz) drive this panel on mainline in
ROCKNIX (tag 20261101) through a generic table-driven panel driver.
The table was generated with tools/gen_nv3052c_table.py in
Allwinner-H700-Custom-Kernel-Research from the stock image, which
checks the result against that working file.

The stock sequence waits after exit-sleep before display-on; 120 ms is
used here, as in the working setup above.

This patch was drafted with an AI coding assistant (Claude) and checked
by building with W=1 (arm64, gcc 13.3.0). It has not been tested on
hardware.
---
 .../gpu/drm/panel/panel-newvision-nv3052c.c   | 179 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 179 insertions(+)

